@3020 =~Z's Mythic Spell Notes - Absolute Death~
@3021 =~This book collects the notes of a wizard known only as "Z" on the mythic spells. If you wish, you may study the secrets within.

Note: learning a mythic spell requires the following:
- character level 20 or higher
- a Wisdom score above 22
- permanently losing 1 point of Wisdom and 100,000 experience points when it is learned

Mythic spells are innate abilities and need not be memorized. Studying a mythic spell book again increases the number of uses.

The spell recorded in this book is:

Absolute Death (Mythic)
Level: 10
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: One target
Saving Throw: None

This spell focuses the caster's will into a pure decree of death and turns it directly upon the target's soul. If the target fails a saving throw vs. death at a -4 penalty, it dies instantly, ignoring its creature type and any immunity to death magic. Even on a successful save, the target still takes 100 points of nonlethal damage.

Cost:
The caster must make a saving throw vs. death at a -4 penalty or take 10d6 points of backlash damage.

"Death never negotiates. It only announces."
- Z~

@3022 =~Z's Mythic Spell Notes - Corrupt Magic~
@3023 =~This book collects the notes of a wizard known only as "Z" on the mythic spells. If you wish, you may study the secrets within.

Note: learning a mythic spell requires the following:
- character level 20 or higher
- a Wisdom score above 22
- permanently losing 1 point of Wisdom and 100,000 experience points when it is learned

Mythic spells are innate abilities and need not be memorized. Studying a mythic spell book again increases the number of uses.

The spell recorded in this book is:

Corrupt Magic (Mythic)
Level: 10
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: One target
Saving Throw: None

This spell releases a twisted force of corrupt magic that erodes the target's magical essence. It removes every magical effect on the target, including the effects of spells, potions and some magical items. Spells and spell-like effects are completely unravelled and destroyed, as if the target had been struck by a powerful Dispel Magic. Protections such as Spell Shield and Spell Immunity (Abjuration) are stripped away as well.

Each spell protection removed triggers a small burst of corrupt magic. Everything within the burst takes nonlethal damage equal to the removed spell's level x 1d6 and suffers a -2 penalty to its next saving throws. A creature that fails a saving throw vs. death is knocked down for one round. This spell causes no damage or ill effect to party members.

Cost:
The caster forgets one memorized spell, starting from the highest level.

"Magic is born of order, and returns to chaos."
- Z~

@3024 =~Z's Mythic Spell Notes - Threefold Wish~
@3025 =~This book collects the notes of a wizard known only as "Z" on the mythic spells. If you wish, you may study the secrets within.

Note: learning a mythic spell requires the following:
- character level 20 or higher
- a Wisdom score above 22
- permanently losing 1 point of Wisdom and 100,000 experience points when it is learned

Mythic spells are innate abilities and need not be memorized. Studying a mythic spell book again increases the number of uses.

The spell recorded in this book is:

Threefold Wish (Mythic)
Level: 10
Range: 0
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

This spell lets the caster weave and release three complete Wish spells at the same time. Each wish carries its own full power, so several of the caster's intentions can be realized in a single instant. It is said that only a wizard who has touched the threshold of myth can compress such an enormous weight of wishing into one breath.

Cost:
After casting, two memorized spells are forgotten, starting from the highest level; they must be memorized again before they can be used.

"Three wishes in one thought, and even time whispers - but every echo is paid for with a part of yourself."
- Z~

